From 3d86540b7eeca7700f3699f6adc25ac5702c968b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 03:24:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] Give the attachments one source instead of three

The form offered three ways to attach a file and they disagreed with each other: the
attachments table, an Attachment Gallery field, and Frappe's own attachments panel in the
sidebar. Only the table records what a file is - its type, where the paper original is
filed, whether it is secret - and only the table's rows feed the hash the seal covers. A
user who uploaded through the gallery or the sidebar had nowhere to say which paper it was,
and a reviewer could not tell whether the file belonged to the record.

Delete the gallery field from both DocTypes and hide the sidebar panel from each form's
script. Uploading stays native: the row's own Attach control, or a button that opens the
same frappe.ui.FileUploader widget the sidebar used and appends a row defaulting to
type Attachment.

A sealed record withholds the button and says why, rather than letting an upload fail
validation after the user has already picked a file.
