From 9f597f3c96350115186457cbe70f1499836e2c0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 03:27:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] Print the referral's attachments on the slip that
 carries them

The correspondence record listed its attachments; the referral notification - the paper
actually handed to the recipient and signed back - listed none. Somebody signing for a
referral had no written record of the papers travelling with it, and the format's own
stated rule ("a print never exposes a file the printing user cannot open") was applied to
the parent correspondence while its own attachment names went straight onto the page.

The slip now prints the same table the record does: number, type, file name, secret
marker, plus a count of what is withheld and a line telling the recipient to request those
from the archive rather than assume nothing was attached.

The stored attachment types are English Select options, so both formats now map them to
Arabic with the stored value as the fallback - the same rule the templates already applied
to direction and activity values but not to attachment types.

The rule that decides whether a name is printed is now asserted for both formats, and a
render pass backs the parse check: the templates are exercised with a record carrying one
ordinary and one secret attachment, so a redaction regression fails the suite instead of
reaching paper.
