From 6272ce63cab250519ce8fa29af2559f1c841c880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 03:52:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] Bring the panel's uploads into the table, and stop them
 being erased on save

A file uploaded from the form's attachments panel was filed in the record's table by the File
event, but the open form never learned about the row. That is not a display lag: Frappe syncs
a child table by deleting every row the submitted document does not contain, so the next save
of that form removed the row the event had just created.

The form now wraps frappe.ui.form.Attachments.attachment_uploaded - the method the panel runs
for every completed upload - and merges the server's rows into frm.doc.attachments. The merge
is additive: a row the user added or edited without saving carries no server name and is kept
as it is, a row that came from the server is copied without __islocal so saving does not insert
it twice, and the form is never reloaded, so nothing typed is discarded.

This also replaces the hook the previous commit shipped, which was dead code. The panel hands
frappe.ui.FileUploader its own on_success - which calls attachment_uploaded - and never reads
one set on the control, so a hook there could never fire. Verified in
frappe/public/js/frappe/form/sidebar/attachments.js.

Two smaller corrections:

* A failure to file the row no longer aborts the upload. The file is already stored and the
  seal still covers it through the linked-file snapshot, so raising there would roll the whole
  request back and lose the file. The failure is logged and the backfill picks it up later.
* The backfill query no longer names a limit argument, since frappe.get_all is already the
  unpaginated read and get_list is the paginated one.
