From d1e1f0dbf765f6ad1e3a5c01002f3dc08ba22f11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 05:56:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] fix(reports): print the A4 layout, and render it in the
 engine that actually runs

Printing or exporting any of the three management reports produced Frappe's
default grid instead of the shipped A4 layout. Three independent causes, all of
them in how the framework chooses a report template:

* query_report.js::get_print_template returns "print_grid" whenever the report
  has no template of its own, and the template it looks for is
  <module>/report/<report>/<report>.html - a file this app never shipped. The
  layout now ships next to each report, so Print and PDF use it with no dialog
  step.
* The three Print Format rows declared print_format_type "Jinja", but the report
  print dialog lists only "JS" formats (its get_query filters on exactly that),
  so they could not be selected either. A browser-rendered report layout is a JS
  format; the rows now say so.
* The layout itself was written for Jinja, and a report layout is rendered by
  frappe/public/js/frappe/microtemplate.js. {% set %}, {% elif %}, `in`,
  filters and `or` compile to invalid JavaScript there - selecting the format
  would have printed nothing at all - and {% if data %} is true for an empty
  list, because an empty array is truthy in JavaScript. The layout now sticks
  to the engine's grammar, and tests/render_report_template.mjs executes it in
  that engine: Jinja accepted the old template, which is exactly why the defect
  reached a printout.

One source for the layout (the report folder), no second copy in the JSON, and
the installer now refreshes a Print Format whose template went stale so a
corrected layout reaches a site that installed the format earlier. Thirty
missing Arabic labels for the reports, their columns and their KPI cards are
added, and ar.csv had one malformed row.
