Subject: [PATCH 13/17] docs: add the launch acceptance sheet

One sheet to walk a real site through before users touch it: preparation, the
full correspondence and referral lifecycle, sealing and reopening, attachments,
both record print formats, the three report layouts, the thirteen reports, the
three roles, and the form panels and list indicators.

Every expected result is grounded in the shipped code and in the Arabic refusal
messages in ar.csv, so a mismatch is a named symptom rather than a description.
Sections 10 and 11 ask for the two lists that pay for the walkthrough - what
rendered in English on an Arabic screen, and what never appeared - and state
plainly what the sheet cannot prove, including that no Frappe runtime exists
where these branches were authored.
