From b31f81f73986ffe28b4d77de166fd643a5e3aad2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:22:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] fix(notifications): reach the due day itself, and name
 the type the way Frappe does

A review of the shipped mechanism against the five questions and against each role
found two real defects and one silent hole.

Notification Type is autonamed `field:type_name` and its data field is `type_name` -
not `notification_type`, which is the Notification's own field. Naming it wrong threw
inside the insert and downgraded every reminder to the framework's plain "Alert",
which also means a user could no longer mute the referral reminders on their own:
Frappe ships Notification Type Preference, and a type that is never created cannot be
switched off. Verified by executing the creation path: the three rows now carry
type_name.

The due date itself was silent. A one-day lead time and a one-day grace leave the day
the work is actually owed with nothing sent - the framework matches the date field
exactly, so "before" and "after" cannot cover "on". A third reminder at offset 0 closes
it, and the budget stays bounded: three per referral, one per day, none repeating.

plan() created a Notification Type. A report an administrator runs to check a site must
not configure it, so the read path now takes create=False.

docs/NOTIFICATION_REVIEW.md records the review: the five questions, what is covered,
the two fixes, the seven remaining gaps with their impact and status - including that
Murasalat Approval Request has lifecycle methods declared but no workflow created by
any command in this app, so an approval waiting for a user notifies nobody and may
have no reachable action at all - and a per-role verdict on sufficiency.
