From 8bf9e5cc8779194df8e6d4103d99e7e60e990282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:27:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] feat(workflows, notifications): close the reachable
 gaps, and say why the rest stay open

Three gaps from docs/NOTIFICATION_REVIEW.md are now closed, each through the surface
Frappe already provides.

The Approval Workflow did not exist. services/approvals.py shipped stamp_approval and
clear_approval, declared them in workflow_methods, and documented attaching them to a
"Murasalat Approval Workflow" - but nothing in this app created that workflow, so an
approval had no state, no transition, and no way to run either method. Question five -
is a formal action waiting for me - was answerable for correspondences and referrals and
unanswerable for approvals. It is now a two-state, two-transition workflow: Pending
Approval -> Approve -> Approved (Stamp Approval), and Approved -> Return for Amendment
-> Pending Approval (Clear Approval). Two states rather than three because every
transition must carry its task - the invariant the whole governance model rests on - and
a "Submit for Approval" transition has no lifecycle method to carry.

Cancellation was unreachable. cancel_referral shipped with its mandatory reason, its
refusal on a completed referral and its activity entry, and OPEN/DONE conditions in the
notifications keyed on cancelled_on - but no transition ever called it. A Cancelled state
and three Cancel transitions now exist, with Cancel Referral declared in workflow_methods
and attached, so cancelling closes the ToDo and stops the reminders.

The sender was never told. Two native Value Change rules on workflow_state now notify the
record's own owner field when a referral is received and when it is completed - the
framework's supported way to name a recipient from the record. Value Change fires only on
an actual change, so each is written at most once with no guard, and the framework already
skips a notice when the actor is the person being told.

The review document records what was closed and what stays open with its reason: a
department-targeted referral still notifies nobody (no recipient can be derived without
either broadcasting or inventing an owner), the correspondence due_date has no owner in
the model, escalation needs two policy decisions the code cannot make, and per-recipient
language is impossible on this channel because the framework renders the message once per
send in the job's session language.
